<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17150" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex-pŭto</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To lop off</i>, <i>to prune</i>, <i>to crop</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">veteranam vitem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					3, 15, 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">5, 6, 31</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">palos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					11, 2, 12</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>To consider well</i>, <i>to
			examine</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">utramque rem simul,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Trin. 2, 1, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">id exputando evolvere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Auct. Her. 2, 26, 42</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>To fathom</i>, <i>comprehend</i>:
			quae mens eum aut quorum consilia a tanta gloria avocarint, exputare
			non possum, Planc. ap. <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam. 10, 24, 6</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
